/-!
# Extending a line bundle from the generic fibre of a smooth DVR scheme

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BD9 (`lemma-extend-invertible-module`),
Descent, Tag 036D, and More on Algebra, Tag 0AG0
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-dvr-generic-line-extension).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Every invertible module on the generic fibre of a smooth finite type scheme over a
DVR extends to an invertible module on the entire scheme. The restriction is pullback
along the first projection of the fibre product. This is an existence statement only.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BD9 (`lemma-extend-invertible-module`),
Descent, Tag 036D, and More on Algebra, Tag 0AG0
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-dvr-generic-line-extension).

Proof:
1. A DVR is Noetherian, local of dimension one, and regular: its maximal ideal is
   generated by a uniformizer (def-sc-discrete-valuation-ring,
   lem-sc-dvr-dimension-one, def-weil-regular-scheme). Its two prime localizations
   are itself and its fraction field, so it is a regular ring.
2. Smooth affine charts lie over affine opens of Spec R, whose rings are R or K.
   Convert scheme smoothness to ring smoothness by
   lem-weil-pbc-smooth-ring-map-iff-smooth-affine and use
   lem-weil-pbc-regular-ring-smooth-ascent. Thus Y is regular and locally Noetherian.
   Finite type makes Y quasi-compact, so choose finitely many such affine charts.
3. The stalks are localizations of those regular coordinate rings by
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization. They are regular local, hence UFDs
   by lem-trf-regular-local-ufd-boundary-factorization with r = 0 (choose a full
   regular system of parameters; the selected subfamily is empty).
4. By lem-weil-pbc-dvr-unit-times-uniformizer-power, every nonzero denominator is
   a unit times a power of the uniformizer, so K = R[1/pi]. The generic fibre is
   an open subscheme U of Y by lem-weil-pbc-principal-localization-open-immersion
   and lem-weil-pbc-open-immersion-base-change.
5. Extend over the finite affine charts successively. The intersection of the
   current open with the next chart is Noetherian by
   lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-open-subscheme-noetherian, and is quasi-affine.
   By lem-sfb-quasiaffine-line-effective-divisor its line bundle is O(D) for
   an effective Cartier divisor D. The intersection need not be affine.
6. Extend D over the chart by lem-sfb-cartier-extension-factorial-complement,
   since the local rings on the complement are UFDs. The associated invertible
   module restricts to O(D): locally its dual ideal generator is the inverse of
   a nonzerodivisor, and these generators restrict compatibly
   (def-pc-divisor-line-bundle, def-sc-invertible-module).
7. Glue the old extension and this chart's module along that isomorphism by
   lem-weil-pbc-site-module-sheaf-gluing. The reverse transition is its inverse,
   and the cocycle is cancellation. Local rank one is preserved by gluing.
   Retain the isomorphism on U at each step; the final open is Y. For empty Y,
   its structure sheaf gives the extension. No uniqueness is required.
-/
theorem exists_invertible_extension_of_smooth_dvr
    (R K : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
    [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    (Y : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R))
    [Smooth f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (L : (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R K)))).Modules)
    [L.IsInvertible] :
    ∃ M : Y.Modules, M.IsInvertible ∧
      Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback
        (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R K))))).obj M ≅ L) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
